Third-party components and ported code. Every entry here is also named in the app's About screen.

Cryptomator cryptolib (https://github.com/cryptomator/cryptolib)
  Copyright (C) Skymatic GmbH. Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0.
  Used as a library for the Cryptomator vault format 8 (masterkey file, file headers, chunked
  AES-GCM content, AES-SIV file names). Its transitive dependencies siv-mode (MIT), Gson
  (Apache-2.0), Guava (Apache-2.0) and slf4j-api (MIT) ship with it.

Cryptomator desktop (https://github.com/cryptomator/cryptomator), GPL-3.0:
  - the 4096-word English recovery-key dictionary (src/main/resources/i18n/4096words_en.txt),
    reproduced in shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/info/piepgras/cryptvault/recovery/RecoveryWords.kt;
  - the word encoding and the recovery-key checksum layout (WordEncoder.java,
    RecoveryKeyFactory.java), ported to Kotlin in the same package.
  Origin commit: e1d83c996e501649b2253741e4a80ce54646b317. Attribution is repeated at the top of
  each ported file.

OkHttp and Okio (https://square.github.io/okhttp/), Apache-2.0: the HTTP client of the WebDAV
backup target (Phase 4); also the engine behind Ktor.

zip4j (https://github.com/srikanth-lingala/zip4j), Apache-2.0: ZIP containers with AES-256 (Phase 5).
kage (https://github.com/android-password-store/kage), Apache-2.0: age containers (Phase 5).
PGPainless (https://pgpainless.org), Apache-2.0, and Bouncy Castle (https://www.bouncycastle.org),
MIT-style licence: OpenPGP containers (Phase 5).

Components added by later phases are appended here in the commit that adds them:
Dropbox SDK for Java (MIT), MSAL for Android (MIT), zxcvbn4j (MIT), the EFF long word list
(CC-BY-3.0), and the AndroidX/Kotlin libraries (Apache-2.0).
